Rating guidelines: A company that actively champions liberal democracy, voting rights, and open civic discourse, maintains a workplace that protects employee rights and civil liberties free of executive ideological intimidation, refuses to comply with authoritarian censorship or surveillance demands, and strictly prohibits extremist hate speech, disinformation, and election subversion gets a 100. A company that maintains conventional corporate political neutrality, adheres to statutory civil rights and non-discrimination mandates, avoids direct ties to political extremism, but does not proactively champion democratic institutions or push back against authoritarian government pressure gets a 50. A company whose executives openly finance, endorse, or promote right-wing extremism and anti-democratic candidates, enforces an autocratic workplace culture that retaliates against political dissent, amplifies or monetizes extremist disinformation and hate speech, or directly collaborates with authoritarian regimes to censor dissidents and subvert democratic freedoms gets a 1.